---
<DocsLayout title="Testing" description="How to test and validate the honeypot system" section="Testing" sidebar={sidebar} toc={toc}>
  <h2 id="layers">Testing Layers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Unit / Integration Tests:</strong> Lua module logic, dashboard generation, timeline capture. Pure Lua modules (*_rules.lua) are testable under a plain Lua interpreter without OpenResty.</li>
    <li><strong>Functional Testing:</strong> End-to-end honeypot interaction and detection validation.</li>
    <li><strong>Blind Pentest Evaluation:</strong> Simulated attacker assessments with internal-test secret gating.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="unit">Unit Test Coverage</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Test File</th><th>Module Under Test</th></tr>
    <tr><td>test_pattern_rules.lua</td><td>pattern_rules.lua — URI/header/CVE/automation scoring</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_router_rules.lua</td><td>router_rules.lua — routing predicates, decay, decision trace</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_vulnerability_rules.lua</td><td>vulnerability_rules.lua — CVE pattern matching, exploit kit detection</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_suricata_rules.lua</td><td>suricata_rules.lua — alert parsing, severity scoring, decay</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_abuseipdb_rules.lua</td><td>abuseipdb_rules.lua — report eligibility, categories, comments</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_lua_pattern_utils.lua</td><td>lua_pattern_utils.lua — URL decode, pattern escape, install wizard URI</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_decay_policy.lua</td><td>decay_policy.lua — escalation-aware decay, permaflag</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_ip_rules.lua</td><td>ip_rules.lua — IPv4/IPv6 CIDR matching</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_upload_rules.lua</td><td>upload_rules.lua — content type, parameters, endpoints, bypass</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_admin_rules.lua</td><td>admin_rules.lua — login, patterns, brute force, credential stuffing</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_session_rules.lua</td><td>session_rules.lua — anomalies, honeypot routing</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_session_identity_rules.lua</td><td>session_identity_rules.lua — cookie signing, fingerprinting, rejections</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_honeytoken_rules.lua</td><td>honeytoken_rules.lua — token-in-corpus matching</td></tr>
