    <tr><td>test_router_decide_route.lua</td><td>router.lua — routing decision pipeline</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_gdpr_rules.lua</td><td>gdpr_rules.lua — timestamp, canonical chars, validation</td></tr>
    <tr><td>test_pool_assignment.lua</td><td>pool_router.lua — pool assignment lifecycle</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2 id="dashboard">Dashboard Tests</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>dashboard/tests/test_kibana_dashboards.py</code> — Validates NDJSON dashboard integrity against build_dashboards.py output.</li>
    <li><code>dashboard/tests/test_host_settings.py</code> — Host settings validation.</li>
    <li><code>dashboard/tests/test_overview_stats.py</code> — Overview stats validation.</li>
    <li><code>dashboard/tests/test_learning.py</code> — Learning page validation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="secret">Internal Test Secret</h2>
  <p>The <code>INTERNAL_TEST_SECRET</code> env var gates the <code>X-Route-Target</code> and <code>X-Risk-Score</code> response headers. When set, headers only emitted for requests with matching <code>X-Internal-Test-Auth</code> header. When unset, headers never emitted (fail closed). This allows scenario scripts to verify routing decisions without exposing oracles to real users or blind pentests.</p>

  <h2 id="running">Running Tests</h2>
  <pre><code># Lua unit tests (plain Lua interpreter, no OpenResty needed)
cd ids/reverse_proxy_enhanced/lua && lua tests/test_&lt;module&gt;.lua

# Dashboard tests
cd dashboard && python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v

# Scenario tests
bash testing/scenario_*.sh</code></pre>

  <h2 id="honest">Honest Assessment</h2>
  <p><strong>Strengths:</strong> Pure/adapter split enables 18 unit test files. Comprehensive coverage of all pure modules. Dashboard validation catches NDJSON drift.</p>
  <p><strong>Limitations:</strong> No end-to-end integration tests. Blind pentest requires manual setup. No CI/CD integration. Sophistication classifier and honeytoken handler lack dedicated tests.</p>
</DocsLayout>
